@startuml
title cgroup v2 — Unified Hierarchy and Controller Delegation
rectangle "Root cgroup" as root
rectangle "Course / workload subtree" as parent
rectangle "Container A cgroup" as a
rectangle "Container B cgroup" as b
root --> parent : hierarchical limits
parent --> a : child membership
parent --> b : child membership
note right of root
Available controllers (examples): cpu, memory, io, pids.
Enable applicable controllers in cgroup.subtree_control.
Limits and delegation constraints apply down the hierarchy.
end note
note bottom of parent
Controllers are capabilities of the hierarchy, not child cgroups.
Namespace view, membership and resource limits are distinct concepts.
end note
@enduml
